1
00:00:13,931 --> 00:00:14,765
Oh, well...

2
00:00:27,319 --> 00:00:28,696
Wait-- What's going on?

3
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:32,324
Seriously, don't just barge in like that!

4
00:00:32,408 --> 00:00:33,576
Sorry!

5
00:00:35,870 --> 00:00:38,164
Why do I have to apologize?

6
00:00:38,247 --> 00:00:40,332
You'll be in trouble if you catch a cold!

7
00:00:40,916 --> 00:00:43,169
That's a whole different story!

8
00:00:43,252 --> 00:00:45,546
"We won't invade each other's territory."

9
00:00:45,629 --> 00:00:47,673
We agreed when we got to 6th grade, right?

10
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:51,677
What the heck?

11
00:00:53,888 --> 00:00:55,222
Hey, Yu.

12
00:00:55,306 --> 00:00:56,348
What is it?

13
00:00:57,057 --> 00:00:58,934
Thanks for the blanket.

14
00:02:32,278 --> 00:02:33,946
{\an8}DEVILS' CREST

15
00:02:34,029 --> 00:02:37,908
{\an8}EPISODE 3: AWAKENING

16
00:02:41,912 --> 00:02:45,958
I'm sure everyone from Class 1
is barricaded inside.

17
00:02:46,041 --> 00:02:47,418
We have to do something.

18
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:50,796
That won't work.

19
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:54,091
That guy probably has really high HP
and physical defense.

20
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:55,676
But we can't just leave it.

21
00:02:56,427 --> 00:02:57,761
I know.

22
00:02:57,845 --> 00:02:59,847
We have to fight using magic,

23
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:02,850
but my MP hasn't even
recovered to half yet.

24
00:03:03,517 --> 00:03:06,437
<i>Think. How can we beat it?</i>

25
00:03:06,979 --> 00:03:09,148
<i>Even if the system works like in the game,</i>

26
00:03:09,231 --> 00:03:11,400
<i>there are no weapon or item shops here.</i>

27
00:03:12,276 --> 00:03:15,279
<i>This is reality. Actual reality.</i>

28
00:03:21,035 --> 00:03:23,537
Sawa, Konken, can you guys escape...

29
00:03:23,621 --> 00:03:26,332
No, wait, can you run around it
for just a minute?

30
00:03:28,667 --> 00:03:29,501
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

31
00:03:29,585 --> 00:03:31,170
But what are you planning?

32
00:03:31,253 --> 00:03:32,504
Let me handle it for now.

33
00:03:40,179 --> 00:03:41,472
I'll grab aggro.

34
00:03:41,555 --> 00:03:43,474
Cover me from the side.

35
00:03:43,557 --> 00:03:44,433
Got it!

36
00:03:45,935 --> 00:03:47,561
Over here, monster!

37
00:03:49,355 --> 00:03:50,522
Over here, over here!

38
00:03:50,606 --> 00:03:52,107
Hey, what are you looking at?

39
00:03:55,277 --> 00:03:56,111
Go!

40
00:03:58,238 --> 00:03:59,114
Hey!

41
00:04:02,493 --> 00:04:05,871
<i>Sawa, Konken, hang in there!</i>

42
00:04:06,789 --> 00:04:07,748
DOCTOR'S OFFICE

43
00:04:15,714 --> 00:04:16,966
This should be enough.

44
00:04:18,968 --> 00:04:21,136
Hey, demon, over here.

45
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:22,596
Come on, come on!

46
00:04:35,192 --> 00:04:36,151
Take this!

47
00:04:36,986 --> 00:04:38,237
Durendal!

48
00:04:44,952 --> 00:04:45,911
Ouch.

49
00:04:54,670 --> 00:04:55,546
Yu!

50
00:04:58,132 --> 00:04:59,925
Yu, what was that?

51
00:05:00,009 --> 00:05:01,552
Ethanol for disinfection.

52
00:05:01,635 --> 00:05:04,430
I see. So, it's a substitute for magic.

53
00:05:04,513 --> 00:05:05,556
Yeah.

54
00:05:05,639 --> 00:05:07,933
But how will you light it?

55
00:05:09,435 --> 00:05:10,436
Well...

56
00:05:10,519 --> 00:05:12,938
You didn't even think that far?

57
00:05:13,022 --> 00:05:13,897
{\an8}YUMA ASHIHARA
ALTEA

58
00:05:13,981 --> 00:05:15,566
{\an8}If I run for another minute,

59
00:05:15,649 --> 00:05:19,236
{\an8}I should have enough MP restored
to cast one Flame Arrow.

60
00:05:26,702 --> 00:05:29,496
Wait, let me try something first.

61
00:05:30,456 --> 00:05:31,373
Try what?

62
00:05:38,130 --> 00:05:38,964
Now!

63
00:05:45,721 --> 00:05:49,892
CONEHEAD BRUISER

64
00:05:49,975 --> 00:05:52,770
Wow, it's really working!

65
00:05:52,853 --> 00:05:55,814
But it's taking longer to run out
than I thought.

66
00:05:56,356 --> 00:05:58,859
It's just that there's a lot of HP.

67
00:06:05,741 --> 00:06:08,160
CONEHEAD BRUISER

68
00:06:09,328 --> 00:06:13,624
For a monster, this thing
is just like a real living creature...

69
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:17,169
These aren't just 3D objects.

70
00:06:17,878 --> 00:06:20,672
But that's probably only
while they're alive.

71
00:06:22,007 --> 00:06:23,467
What do you mean?

72
00:06:33,769 --> 00:06:35,270
You're kidding!

73
00:06:35,354 --> 00:06:36,688
No way.

74
00:06:37,397 --> 00:06:39,858
With that much left,
a physical attack should...

75
00:06:40,526 --> 00:06:43,487
No, wait, I need to refill
with fresh ethanol.

76
00:06:49,159 --> 00:06:50,077
Yu!

77
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:51,578
Yuumy!

78
00:06:52,955 --> 00:06:54,206
Let me go!

79
00:07:01,922 --> 00:07:02,798
Yu!

80
00:07:03,423 --> 00:07:04,675
Stop it!

81
00:07:13,517 --> 00:07:15,144
Get away now, Yu!

82
00:07:19,106 --> 00:07:19,940
Let him go!

83
00:07:20,023 --> 00:07:22,317
Don't give up, Yuumy!

84
00:07:25,904 --> 00:07:27,573
YUMA ASHIHARA

85
00:07:48,427 --> 00:07:49,595
Where am I?

86
00:07:53,849 --> 00:07:56,727
The stars are... falling.

87
00:07:58,020 --> 00:07:58,937
That's right.

88
00:08:00,314 --> 00:08:03,358
That's what you call the P-T Boundary.

89
00:08:04,026 --> 00:08:08,113
It's the very thing that triggered the
largest mass extinction in Earth's history

90
00:08:08,197 --> 00:08:10,324
at the end of the Permian period.

91
00:08:11,742 --> 00:08:17,247
Soon, 95% of all life on this planet
will be wiped out.

92
00:08:17,748 --> 00:08:19,791
Oh, no! We've got to do something!

93
00:08:21,293 --> 00:08:22,878
Unfortunately, there's no way.

94
00:08:24,087 --> 00:08:28,383
At this point,
neither angels nor devils can stop it.

95
00:08:28,467 --> 00:08:31,136
Angels? Devils?

96
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:36,975
Besides, this happened
250 million years ago.

97
00:08:38,352 --> 00:08:40,437
If it weren't for that mass extinction,

98
00:08:41,021 --> 00:08:45,234
you modern humans wouldn't exist, Yuma.

99
00:08:45,734 --> 00:08:48,278
Who are you?

100
00:08:49,363 --> 00:08:51,573
Should you really be
worrying about that now?

101
00:08:52,157 --> 00:08:55,035
You're on the verge of death right now.

102
00:08:56,745 --> 00:08:59,331
Am I dead?

103
00:08:59,831 --> 00:09:02,000
The thread of life is still connected.

104
00:09:03,627 --> 00:09:07,130
But how on earth
could I have survived that?

105
00:09:07,214 --> 00:09:09,591
Adjust the angle of the rod

106
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:12,761
and use the Monster Tamer's power.

107
00:09:14,054 --> 00:09:15,514
At the same time.

108
00:09:16,098 --> 00:09:17,683
How do you know all this?

109
00:09:18,976 --> 00:09:20,394
It doesn't matter right now.

110
00:09:21,019 --> 00:09:24,022
Do you want to live?
Or will you accept death?

111
00:09:25,023 --> 00:09:28,902
That monster is going to kill
your friend and your sister, too.

112
00:09:32,072 --> 00:09:34,408
Okay. I'll do it.

113
00:09:34,491 --> 00:09:35,575
Good.

114
00:09:36,076 --> 00:09:38,161
I bet on you, after all.

115
00:09:39,371 --> 00:09:41,206
Now, wake up.

116
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:45,210
Three, two, one...

117
00:09:58,432 --> 00:09:59,474
Aperta!

118
00:10:28,628 --> 00:10:30,297
CONEHEAD BRUISER

119
00:10:37,137 --> 00:10:38,180
Yuumy!

120
00:10:39,139 --> 00:10:40,265
I'm fine.

121
00:11:01,161 --> 00:11:02,329
Sumika!

122
00:11:02,412 --> 00:11:03,455
Watamaki...

123
00:11:04,164 --> 00:11:06,541
Watamaki is my familiar.

124
00:11:07,417 --> 00:11:11,880
At the very least,
she shouldn't see us as targets.

125
00:11:15,592 --> 00:11:16,885
Yuumy!

126
00:11:26,103 --> 00:11:30,524
I'm... coming...

127
00:11:31,149 --> 00:11:32,150
<i>I knew it.</i>

128
00:11:32,234 --> 00:11:35,862
<i>Deep down somewhere,
the real Watamaki is there.</i>

129
00:11:45,997 --> 00:11:47,624
Thank you, Watamaki.

130
00:11:48,166 --> 00:11:50,210
I promise to bring you back to yourself.

131
00:11:52,379 --> 00:11:53,505
Clause.

132
00:12:06,059 --> 00:12:08,520
{\an8}ALTEA 1F

133
00:12:08,603 --> 00:12:10,897
But this is the real world...

134
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:13,358
All right, we leveled up!

135
00:12:14,234 --> 00:12:16,862
Yu, you leveled up too, right?

136
00:12:16,945 --> 00:12:19,448
So, does that mean
if we land even a single hit,

137
00:12:19,531 --> 00:12:21,783
we split the experience point evenly?

138
00:12:21,867 --> 00:12:23,827
It's the same as Actual Magic.

139
00:12:24,995 --> 00:12:25,871
BRUISING HAMMER

140
00:12:25,954 --> 00:12:29,416
The Item Drop log is shown
along with the Level Up log.

141
00:12:29,499 --> 00:12:31,793
The drop? Seriously?

142
00:12:32,335 --> 00:12:34,421
If it's the same as Actual Magic,

143
00:12:34,504 --> 00:12:36,006
it should be in the inventory.

144
00:12:36,089 --> 00:12:37,299
TEST PASS CERTIFICATE CARD

145
00:12:37,924 --> 00:12:41,344
I see. So, we have an inventory
in this world too, huh?

146
00:12:42,012 --> 00:12:43,513
It was very powerful.

147
00:12:43,597 --> 00:12:46,141
I bet you got a pretty good item,
didn't you?

148
00:12:46,224 --> 00:12:48,310
The test pass certificate card...

149
00:12:48,393 --> 00:12:50,812
A card you got at the playtest, huh?

150
00:12:50,896 --> 00:12:53,064
Monster card, Squeak!

151
00:12:54,316 --> 00:12:56,443
Squeak? That one?

152
00:12:56,526 --> 00:13:00,030
The weapons and armor I got
during the playtest are gone,

153
00:13:00,113 --> 00:13:01,448
so why do I have Squeak?

154
00:13:01,531 --> 00:13:03,450
Hey, isn't this a potion?

155
00:13:05,535 --> 00:13:07,204
LESSER HP POTION

156
00:13:10,749 --> 00:13:12,209
Lesser potions, really?

157
00:13:12,292 --> 00:13:14,419
Even lesser potions are precious.

158
00:13:15,170 --> 00:13:17,714
Unlike real-world medicine or bandages,

159
00:13:17,797 --> 00:13:20,133
it heals you instantly
the moment you drink it.

160
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,010
Probably.

161
00:13:22,093 --> 00:13:23,470
Well, I guess so.

162
00:13:23,553 --> 00:13:24,554
Thanks.

163
00:13:29,309 --> 00:13:31,061
Okay, I got it.

164
00:13:31,144 --> 00:13:32,062
Me too.

165
00:13:33,813 --> 00:13:34,898
If we go outside,

166
00:13:34,981 --> 00:13:38,985
we might be able to ask the police
or the fire department for help.

167
00:13:39,069 --> 00:13:41,738
But the automatic doors won't open, right?

168
00:13:41,821 --> 00:13:43,490
Konken, use this.

169
00:13:43,573 --> 00:13:44,491
BRUISING HAMMER

170
00:13:45,992 --> 00:13:47,994
You got a weapon too?

171
00:13:48,578 --> 00:13:50,830
All right, leave this to me!

172
00:13:57,087 --> 00:13:58,755
Hey, are you okay?

173
00:14:00,882 --> 00:14:02,509
What the heck is this?

174
00:14:03,093 --> 00:14:05,845
I guess it's protected
by some kind of magic.

175
00:14:06,471 --> 00:14:10,475
I don't think there's anything we can do
to break this glass right now.

176
00:14:10,559 --> 00:14:11,476
Magic?

177
00:14:12,394 --> 00:14:13,478
The other glass too.

178
00:14:14,104 --> 00:14:17,148
No, every wall and door
is probably the same.

179
00:14:18,108 --> 00:14:21,528
So, we're completely trapped, huh?

180
00:14:21,611 --> 00:14:23,780
Can't we get out of Altea?

181
00:14:32,622 --> 00:14:34,040
It'll be okay.

182
00:14:34,124 --> 00:14:38,169
If it's magic, there must be a way
to dispel it, right?

183
00:14:38,795 --> 00:14:40,255
First, let's find Nagi

184
00:14:40,338 --> 00:14:42,299
and get Watamaki back to herself.

185
00:14:44,259 --> 00:14:45,302
Yu...

186
00:14:46,303 --> 00:14:47,887
Of course, we will!

187
00:14:47,971 --> 00:14:50,849
Let's get our party of four
back together ASAP!

188
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:57,230
Guess we'll head back, then.

189
00:14:57,314 --> 00:15:00,692
We've got to tell the guys in Class 1
that it's safe now.

190
00:15:00,775 --> 00:15:02,527
Wait, before we do that,

191
00:15:03,194 --> 00:15:05,905
let's just form a party
with us three for now.

192
00:15:06,448 --> 00:15:08,491
We can see each other's HP,

193
00:15:08,575 --> 00:15:11,202
and we'll get experience points
even if we don't fight.

194
00:15:11,286 --> 00:15:12,162
FRIEND REQUEST

195
00:15:14,372 --> 00:15:15,373
WILL YOU JOIN?

196
00:15:15,457 --> 00:15:16,291
You bet!

197
00:15:16,374 --> 00:15:18,752
If the monster shows up again,

198
00:15:18,835 --> 00:15:22,172
I'm gonna knock it out cold
with my physical power.

199
00:15:26,593 --> 00:15:28,303
SAWA ASHIHARA

200
00:15:29,763 --> 00:15:30,764
{\an8}ALTEA 1F

201
00:15:30,847 --> 00:15:31,681
{\an8}What is it?

202
00:15:32,223 --> 00:15:34,059
Well, never mind.

203
00:15:34,142 --> 00:15:35,268
Hey, Yu.

204
00:15:35,977 --> 00:15:37,187
What is it?

205
00:15:37,270 --> 00:15:40,315
Where did you find
that ethanol from earlier?

206
00:15:41,566 --> 00:15:42,734
In the back room.

207
00:15:43,902 --> 00:15:44,944
I see.

208
00:15:45,654 --> 00:15:48,323
Konken, will you go ahead
to where everyone is?

209
00:15:49,532 --> 00:15:51,576
What about you two?

210
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:54,162
I'm dressed like this, you know?

211
00:15:54,245 --> 00:15:55,955
I want to find something to wear.

212
00:15:58,708 --> 00:15:59,834
That's true.

213
00:15:59,918 --> 00:16:01,461
Then I'll go ahead.

214
00:16:02,671 --> 00:16:03,546
Please.

215
00:16:10,637 --> 00:16:13,473
Weren't you supposed
to be looking for your clothes?

216
00:16:13,556 --> 00:16:14,974
Why are we in the infirmary?

217
00:16:15,558 --> 00:16:16,726
Show me.

218
00:16:21,272 --> 00:16:23,900
That's a relief. It's a shallow cut.

219
00:16:24,526 --> 00:16:26,152
I'll disinfect it just in case.

220
00:16:29,948 --> 00:16:33,368
TEST PASS CERTIFICATE CARD
MONSTER CARD - SQUEAK

221
00:16:33,451 --> 00:16:35,370
DISINFECTANT

222
00:16:35,954 --> 00:16:37,205
I knew it!

223
00:16:37,288 --> 00:16:40,417
Looks like you can store
real-world items in the storage too.

224
00:16:41,543 --> 00:16:44,754
Yu, open your storage
and put everything here in there.

225
00:16:46,172 --> 00:16:47,132
Okay.

226
00:16:57,183 --> 00:16:58,852
- Break the glass?
- Yes.

227
00:16:59,519 --> 00:17:02,147
No way. Even if it is an emergency...

228
00:17:02,939 --> 00:17:04,733
Yu, calm down and listen.

229
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:08,403
I don't think we'll be able
to get out of here for a while.

230
00:17:08,486 --> 00:17:09,946
How long?

231
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:12,157
Two or three days, maybe ten,

232
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:13,575
or possibly even longer.

233
00:17:15,410 --> 00:17:18,621
Come on, it can't be that long.

234
00:17:19,122 --> 00:17:21,916
There must be a huge commotion
outside by now.

235
00:17:23,752 --> 00:17:26,921
If we used a bulldozer or something,
even that glass would surely...

236
00:17:27,005 --> 00:17:28,673
You already know, right?

237
00:17:28,757 --> 00:17:30,258
Altea is currently

238
00:17:30,341 --> 00:17:33,511
being gradually overtaken
by the world of Actual Magic.

239
00:17:35,638 --> 00:17:37,557
What if the glass were reinforced

240
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:40,643
with some kind of top-tier magic
powerful enough to stop a meteorite?

241
00:17:41,227 --> 00:17:43,354
Do you think a bulldozer could smash that?

242
00:17:45,482 --> 00:17:47,859
Anyway, I'm not stockpiling just for now.

243
00:17:48,359 --> 00:17:52,572
A safe shelter, food, water, and medicine,

244
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:55,033
those are going to be really important.

245
00:17:55,867 --> 00:17:57,786
There'll definitely be trouble eventually.

246
00:17:58,369 --> 00:18:00,497
Are you trying to hog it all
for ourselves?

247
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:01,790
No!

248
00:18:01,873 --> 00:18:04,751
I'm securing it
before someone else grabs it

249
00:18:04,834 --> 00:18:06,711
and making sure it's shared fairly.

250
00:18:06,795 --> 00:18:08,505
Then it doesn't have to be now--

251
00:18:08,588 --> 00:18:10,673
I don't want to regret it
when it's too late!

252
00:18:15,386 --> 00:18:18,264
Besides, if we have medicine and food,

253
00:18:18,348 --> 00:18:21,684
we'll be in a better position
if we have to negotiate with someone.

254
00:18:28,316 --> 00:18:31,736
Are you... really Sawa?

255
00:18:32,403 --> 00:18:33,863
What?

256
00:18:34,948 --> 00:18:36,616
Okay, I get it.

257
00:18:36,699 --> 00:18:39,244
Let's put as much as we can
into the storage.

258
00:18:41,538 --> 00:18:44,541
I can't get the stuff inside
without breaking the glass.

259
00:18:44,624 --> 00:18:48,378
But I really don't want the food
to get covered in glass shards.

260
00:18:49,128 --> 00:18:51,005
Then why don't we experiment?

261
00:18:51,631 --> 00:18:52,507
Experiment?

262
00:18:55,385 --> 00:18:57,512
I'll try putting this into storage.

263
00:19:08,857 --> 00:19:11,776
Wow! The dirt came off!

264
00:19:11,860 --> 00:19:14,487
Yeah. I was thinking
that anything other than items

265
00:19:14,571 --> 00:19:17,407
might not be allowed by the system.

266
00:19:17,490 --> 00:19:20,410
I see. Good thinking, Yu!

267
00:19:26,791 --> 00:19:30,086
At least we're all set for water, food,
and medicine for now.

268
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:33,047
Thanks for your help, Yu.

269
00:19:34,549 --> 00:19:36,676
Could you stick around a little longer?

270
00:19:40,013 --> 00:19:41,431
WOMEN'S LOCKER ROOM

271
00:19:41,514 --> 00:19:43,433
Well, it's pretty big.

272
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:48,938
But that's actually a good thing.
I can hide my wings in it.

273
00:19:49,772 --> 00:19:51,107
Let's go back to the lobby--

274
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:52,692
Wait, hold up, Sawa!

275
00:19:54,235 --> 00:19:58,448
Konken and I just got a bigger QREST,

276
00:19:58,531 --> 00:20:00,992
but for only you
to grow something like that...

277
00:20:01,075 --> 00:20:02,911
It just doesn't make any sense!

278
00:20:05,246 --> 00:20:06,414
Can you come over?

279
00:20:13,004 --> 00:20:15,298
Hey, where did you get that?

280
00:20:15,381 --> 00:20:16,841
Inside the locker.

281
00:20:16,925 --> 00:20:18,509
But look closely.

282
00:20:23,181 --> 00:20:25,433
My hair is blue!

283
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:27,644
It's not just me.

284
00:20:28,227 --> 00:20:31,272
To varying degrees,
your body is changing too.

285
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:34,567
Probably Konken
and everyone else in the class as well.

286
00:20:37,153 --> 00:20:39,155
I feel a lump...

287
00:20:40,823 --> 00:20:42,075
What is this?

288
00:20:43,368 --> 00:20:46,746
Could we be going through the same thing
that happened to Watamaki?

289
00:20:47,288 --> 00:20:49,457
Will we end up like that someday too?

290
00:20:50,249 --> 00:20:53,252
<i>I don't think we'll end up like Sumika.</i>

291
00:20:53,962 --> 00:20:56,464
<i>Her transformation
was kind of an exception.</i>

292
00:20:59,384 --> 00:21:00,635
Hey, Sawa,

293
00:21:00,718 --> 00:21:04,055
you know something
you haven't told me yet, don't you?

294
00:21:04,639 --> 00:21:08,142
What's happening to us, to Altea?

295
00:21:13,356 --> 00:21:14,232
Please,

296
00:21:14,983 --> 00:21:16,901
just give me a little more time.

297
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:22,991
Once things calm down,
I'll tell you everything I know.

298
00:21:25,451 --> 00:21:26,661
But right now,

299
00:21:26,744 --> 00:21:29,163
I want to look into it more
and think it over.

300
00:21:30,206 --> 00:21:31,124
So...

301
00:21:33,793 --> 00:21:35,169
Yeah, I get it.

302
00:21:36,421 --> 00:21:39,173
Sorry for making it sound like
I don't trust you.

303
00:21:39,841 --> 00:21:42,927
I know you're doing your best.

304
00:21:49,434 --> 00:21:51,436
Cut the crap!

305
00:21:52,270 --> 00:21:55,189
I bet you're a monster too!

306
00:21:55,273 --> 00:21:56,482
Kondo!

307
00:23:28,032 --> 00:23:28,908
SUSPICION

308
00:23:28,991 --> 00:23:30,952
<i>- What are you saying, Gamo?
- Where's Watamaki?</i>

309
00:23:31,035 --> 00:23:32,078
<i>What makes us monsters?</i>

310
00:23:32,161 --> 00:23:33,121
<i>You didn't kill her...</i>

311
00:23:33,204 --> 00:23:35,665
<i>That was magic, right?</i>

312
00:23:36,165 --> 00:23:37,291
<i>Mo-yan?</i>

313
00:23:37,375 --> 00:23:39,919
<i>Tomochi protected me,</i>

314
00:23:40,711 --> 00:23:42,964
<i>but I left her behind...</i>

315
00:23:43,047 --> 00:23:45,049
Translated by Kanako Murakoshi

